<p>A drone strike caused a fire on Sunday in an electrical generator outside the inner perimeter of the Barakah Nuclear Power Plant in Abu Dhabi’s Al Dhafra region, UAE authorities said. Abu Dhabi officials reported no injuries, no radiological release or increase in radiation levels, and no impact on plant operations. No group immediately claimed responsibility for the strike. Efforts to end the U.S.-Israeli war with Iran and restart shipping in the Gulf remained stalled, and the UAE has hosted Israeli air defences and personnel after Israel attacked Iran with U.S. support on Feb. 28.</p><img src='https://kagiproxy.com/img/MtmK8M9BHD7zOj6FPHJfItPfKrxY1jP5fhYwYv1Rbvzd5gNOtwT4OSvjgfOq0odj4W0Xi2nWIElRcNtyYDPUpTW02EN7syPJ5J7gBgCr0KTas3BNOBWXpxSHGMBPIois4_Bdful0e9GwBo3ZQ9trjaMG0sYLsgUm-twTsXN751wz3uQIP-_LAIdi-iVdtZUMbwEhNWbmoC7_kuS3Mgdw6cBu-GrKhZ6imzLJB6CE-dbCM1S5Zbne-TLLclhqXfGGKUNpYgajoqfuh1Jd-A' alt='A general view of the Barakah Nuclear Power Plant in Abu Dhabi’s western Al Dhafra region.' /><br /><h3>Highlights:</h3><ul><li>First targeting: JNS described the strike as the first time the nation’s only nuclear plant was targeted.</li><li>Threat context: SCMP reported that suspicion immediately fell on Iran because Tehran had increasingly threatened the UAE in recent days.</li><li>Facility profile: Barakah consists of four reactors.</li></ul><blockquote>Military activity that threatens nuclear safety is unacceptable. - Rafael Grossi</blockquote><h3>Perspectives:</h3><ul><li>Abu Dhabi Media Office: The office said authorities responded to the fire and had implemented all precautionary measures. (<a href='https://thepeninsulaqatar.com/article/17/05/2026/drone-strike-causes-fire-outside-abu-dhabi-nuclear-power-plant-no-injuries-reported'>The Peninsula Qatar</a>)</li><li>Federal Authority for Nuclear Regulation: The regulator said the fire did not compromise essential systems’ readiness at the plant. (<a href='https://thepeninsulaqatar.com/article/17/05/2026/drone-strike-